    {
      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "わたしはベトナムのホーチミン市に住んでいたことがあります。",
      "english_translation": "I used to live in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "住む前は、ベトナムの食べ物と言えば「フォー（Phở）」だと思っていました。",
      "english_translation": "Before moving here, when I thought of Vietnamese food, I immediately thought of \"Pho.\""
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "実際、ホーチミンにはたくさんのフォーの店があって、わたしはどの店のフォーもおいしいと思いました。",
      "english_translation": "Actually, there are so many pho restaurants in Ho Chi Minh City, and I thought that every single one of them was delicious."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "ところがある日、ベトナム人の知り合いが「ホーチミンのフォーは、本物のフォーじゃない！」と言いました。",
      "english_translation": "However, one day, I was talking to a Vietnamese friend who said, \"The pho in Ho Chi Minh City isn't authentic!\""
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "その知り合いに聞いたところ、フォーはハノイの名物だそうです。",
      "english_translation": "According to someone I know, pho is a famous dish in Hanoi."
    }
  ],
